      "text": "Hanuman threw mountains at Kumbhakarna. Kumbhakarna hit back with a spear, and Hanuman threw up blood. This happened in the war in Lanka. Kumbhakarna was a giant, and mountains did not stop him. He drove his spear into Hanuman's chest. The Ramayana says Hanuman was badly hurt, with blood coming out of his mouth, but he did not lose. Then Kumbhakarna threw his spear at Sugriva, the monkey king. Hanuman jumped in front of it, caught it, and broke it on his knee. Later, Kumbhakarna caught Sugriva. Hanuman thought of growing as big as a mountain and killing the giant with his fists, but he trusted Sugriva to free himself, and Sugriva did. Kumbhakarna kept fighting until he met Rama. Rama cut off his arms, then his legs, and then his head with one divine arrow. Hanuman threw up blood in that battle, but he never lost. In the end, it took Rama to stop Kumbhakarna.",
