      "text": "The temple is called Gupteshwar Mahadev inside the Asirgarh Fort. Local people say Ashwatthama still comes here every day to pray to Shiva. There is another story from the Narmada River. Travelers say a very tall stranger comes to them. He has a wound on his forehead that never heals. He asks for oil or turmeric to ease the pain. People believe this is Ashwatthama. He has been wandering for thousands of years. He does not ask for money or power. He only asks for relief from his pain. These are stories that people tell. But what do the old books say? In the Mahabharat, Krishna cursed Ashwatthama after he tried to kill an unborn baby. He would wander the Earth for 3,000 years with a wound that never heals. So when people say Ashwatthama still puts flowers on that Shivling every morning, this is the man they mean. A man who tried to kill an unborn baby and was cursed never to find rest.",
