    {
      "text": "Markandeya grew up and loved Shiva with all his heart. On his 16th birthday, Yama came to take his life. The boy was scared. He hugged the Shivling and prayed. Yama threw his rope at the boy, and the rope fell around the Shivling too. This made Shiva very angry. He came out of the Shivling and killed Yama. But now no one was left to take care of death. So the gods begged Shiva to bring Yama back. Shiva did, and he blessed Markandeya to stay 16 forever. Shiva killed Yama, the god of death, to save one 16-year-old boy. Because of this, he is also called Kalantaka, the one who ended Yama.",
