      "text": "The whole universe sits on one hood of Sheshnag, and it is as small as a mustard seed. So, where is he? The Bhagavata Purana tells how the worlds were made. At the start, Vishnu was sleeping on the ocean. A golden lotus came out of his belly button, and Brahma appeared on it. Inside the stem of the lotus, Brahma made 14 worlds, one below the other. The top one is his own world, and the bottom one belongs to the serpents. But when the worlds filled with life, they became too heavy. The stem began to bend, and everything started to fall back into the water. Then Sheshnag appeared with a thousand hoods far below the lowest world. He lifted all 14 worlds on a single hood, and Vishnu, as a giant tortoise, holds Sheshnag up. All 14 worlds sit on his hood like one mustard seed. So our Earth is smaller than a speck of dust on it. So the whole universe sits on one hood of Sheshnag, as small as a mustard seed, and we are even smaller. That is why we cannot see him.",
