      "text": "They are called the Chiranjeevis. The first is Ashwatthama, the son of Drona. He was born with a jewel on his forehead given by Shiva. After the Mahabharata war, he was cursed to wander the earth for thousands of years. The second is Mahabali, who gave everything he had to Vishnu. The third is Vyasa, who wrote the Mahabharata. The fourth is Hanuman, who was blessed with a long life by Rama. The fifth is Vibhishana, Ravana's brother. The sixth is Kripa, a teacher in the Mahabharata. And the seventh is Parashuram, who still lives on Mount Mahendra. So seven beings can never die. Six of them got a gift. Ashwatthama got a punishment that never ends.",
