      "text": "Which weapon is stronger than the Brahmastra? The Brahmastra can stop whole armies, but three weapons are even stronger. First, the Pashupatastra. Shiva gave it to Arjun and warned him, if he used it on a weak enemy, it could burn the whole universe. Arjun did not even need a bow. He could send it with a word, a look, or just a thought and call it back. The Mahabharat says it is greater than the Brahma weapon. Second, Vishnu's Sudarshan Chakra. Ashwatthama had the Brahmashira weapon, but he still wanted Krishna's chakra. Krishna let him try. Ashwatthama used all his strength and could not even lift it. Third, Shiva's trident. The Mahabharat says it is as powerful as the Pashupatastra. In Shiva's hands, it could split the earth, dry up the oceans, and destroy the whole universe. So the Brahmastra, which can stop whole armies, comes after Shiva's Pashupatastra, Vishnu's Sudarshan Chakra, and Shiva's trident. Which one do you think is the strongest?",
