      "text": "We always draw Hanuman with a huge mace, but in the Valmiki Ramayana, he never fights with one. Ravana sent thousands of demons to kill him. Hanuman tore a heavy iron bar out of a gate and used it to destroy them. Then Ravana sent the seven sons of his ministers. Hanuman fought them with his bare hands. He hit some with his palms and some with his feet. In battle, he used his fists, his nails, his chest, and his legs. Some enemies fell to the ground just from the sound of his roar. Hanuman did not need a sword, a bow, or a mace. His strength was his weapon. So the mace we always draw in Hanuman's hand does not appear in his fights in the Valmiki Ramayana. Then why do we always draw him with a mace?",
