      "text": "The Vishnu Purana tells the name of the village where Vishnu's last avatar will be born. It even tells the name of his father. The village is Shambhala. His father is a Brahmin named Vishnuyasha. The child will be Kalki. The same book tells us what the Kali Yuga, our age, will be like. People will be respected for their money, not for their goodness. People will do religion only to show others. Families will stay together only for gain. People will lie in court to win and cheat their own family for money. Which of these is not true today? But the Purana also says how it will end. When evil crosses every limit, Vishnu will be born as Kalki with divine powers. People's minds will become clear and pure, like waking up after a long night. And the last part is the best. In earlier ages, people needed years of meditation, big fire rituals, or long worship. In the Kali Yuga, just saying God's name is enough. So when will Kalki come? When evil crosses every limit in the village of Shambhala, in the house of Vishnuyasha. Until then, God's name is enough.",
